        "original_id": "b8f95244-98e4-5997-ad1c-67cccd82a9b6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Disporum, Boltonia, Disporum viridescens\n- Places: Asia, North America, eastern Asia, northern India, Japan, Indonesia, Russian Far East, Greenwich, Arctic Ocean, Indian Ocean, Southern Ocean, Antarctica, North Pole, South Pole\n- Concepts: genus, species, perennial flowering plants, sunflower family, meridian 72° east\n\nFacts:\n- Disporum is a genus of about 20 species of perennial flowering plants commonly known as fairy bells.\n- Disporum is found in Asia from northern India to Japan, south to Indonesia, and north into the Russian Far East.\n- Boltonia is a genus of plants in the sunflower family native primarily to North America, with one species in eastern Asia.\n- Disporum viridescens is a species of flowering plant in the genus Disporum.\n- The 72nd meridian east of Greenwich is a line of longitude that runs from the North Pole to the South Pole.\n- The 72nd meridian east crosses the Arctic Ocean, Asia, the Indian Ocean, the Southern Ocean, and Antarctica.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
